"n":"Bank of Nova Scotia","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":13.154202,"lo":-61.224341,"d":301},{"n":"Scotiabank","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":13.154202,"lo":-61.224338,"d":301},{"n":"Pharmacy Plus","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":13.153646,"lo":-61.224546,"d":305},{"n":"Bonadie Supermarket #2","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":13.153664,"lo":-61.224337,"d":324},{"n":"Bonadie","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":13.153598,"lo":-61.224269,"d":334},{"n":"Q- Care Pharmacy","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":13.153774,"lo":-61.223757,"d":376,"h":"Mo-Sa 08:00-18:00"},{"n":"Diocese of Kingstown","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.1576,"lo":-61.2289,"d":354,"ds":"The Roman Catholic Diocese of Kingstown (Latin: Dioecesis Regalitana) is a Latin Church ecclesiastical territory or diocese of the Catholic Church in the Caribbean. The diocese comprises the entirety of the nation of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines. The diocese is a suffragan diocese of the Archdiocese of Castries and a member of the Antilles Episcopal Conference.","wpu":"Diocese of Kingstown","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/St._Vincent%2C_Karibik_-_St._Mary%27s_R.C._School_%5E_St._Mary%27s_R.C._Cathedral_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-St._Vincent%2C_Karibik_-_St._Mary%27s_R.C._School_%5E_St._Mary%27s_R.C._Cathedral_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Saint Vincent and the Grenadines Botanic Gardens","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.165833,"lo":-61.227083,"d":1204,"ds":"The Saint Vincent and the Grenadines Botanic Gardens is located in Kingstown, Saint Vincent and the Grenadines. Established in 1765, it is the oldest botanic garden in the Western Hemisphere. It is one of the most visited sites in Saint Vincent and the Grenadines.","wpu":"Saint Vincent and the Grenadines Botanic Gardens","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/03/Breadfruit_drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Geography of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.166667,"lo":-61.233333,"d":1467,"ds":"Saint Vincent and the Grenadines is an island state in the Windward Islands of the Lesser Antilles, an island arc of the Caribbean Sea in North America. The country consists of the main island of Saint Vincent and the northern two-thirds of the Grenadines, a chain of small islands stretching south from Saint Vincent to Grenada. Its total land area is 390 km2 of which 342.7 km2 is the main island of Saint Vincent.","wpu":"Geography of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Saint_Vincent_and_the_Grenadines.svg/960px-Saint_Vincent_and_the_Grenadines.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"LIAT Flight 319","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.137335,"lo":-61.218879,"d":2152,"ds":"LIAT Flight 319 was a scheduled Caribbean inter-island flight from Hewanorra International Airport in Saint Lucia to E. T. Joshua Airport in St. Vincent and the Grenadines.","wpu":"LIAT Flight 319","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/De_Havilland_Canada_DHC-6-300_Twin_Otter%2C_LIAT_AN0208043.jpg/960px-De_Havilland_Canada_DHC-6-300_Twin_Otter%2C_LIAT_AN0208043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Young Island (Grenadines)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.130556,"lo":-61.2025,"d":3798,"ds":"Young Island is one of the smallest islands of Grenadines and part of the state St. Vincent and the Grenadines. It lies immediately south of St.","wpu":"Young Island (Grenadines)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c9/Young_Island_St._Vincent_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Layou","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":13.203333,"lo":-61.268611,"d":7012,"ds":"Layou is a small town located on the island of Saint Vincent, in Saint Andrew Parish. It has two quarries, a post office, a police station and a library.","wpu":"Layou","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0b/SVG-Layou.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Kingstown is the capital and largest city of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines. The city, located on the main island of Saint Vincent, has the main port and the biggest commercial center of the islands. With a population of 12,909 (2012), Kingstown is the most populous settlement in the country.","wpu":"Kingstown","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/Kingstown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}